Lepton: take the decoders' largest picture size from VA-API

The interface accepted pictures up to 4080x4080, so an 8K stream failed to
configure (BAD_VALUE) although the GPU decodes it; VLC then fell back to
software. Query each decodable VA profile's VASurfaceAttribMaxWidth and
MaxHeight once (logged in LEPTON_VA_CAPS as max=TOKEN:WxH). When hardware
decoding is on and VA decodes the codec, the picture-size range is the VA
maximum, otherwise 4080 as before (LEPTON_VA_LIMITS per component).

When that maximum is larger than level 5.x allows (H.264 36864 macroblocks;
HEVC, VP9, AV1 8912896 luma samples), list level 6 as well, so Android's
codec list does not cap the size through the level. Not 6.1 or 6.2: VA
reports no frame rate.

